# Line endings in the WORKING TREE, not just in the index.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows'
# default) materialises CRLF sources, and this repository's gates read their own
# source text: internal/repohygiene, internal/doclint, internal/archguard and a
# dozen reachability checks in internal/mcpserver and cmd/server all parse or
# string-match files on disk. Those matchers hard-code "\n", so on such a host
# they false-alarm on properties that hold — issue #163 measured
# TestSearchResultRendersTheCorrectionMark failing at "could not bound the
# searchHitView literal" over a literal that was there and correct.
#
# `eol=lf` is what fixes the class rather than one matcher. `text=auto` ALONE
# would not: it normalises the INDEX and still hands Windows a CRLF working
# tree, which is exactly the half that breaks, because every gate reads the file
# on disk.
#
# ⚠ THE DEFAULT IS `*`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. An earlier draft listed
# eight extensions and review found the list already incomplete: `.env.example`
# and `.env.docker.example` (read by TestEveryModelACommandDefaultsToIsProvisioned‐
# OrDocumented and by documentedEnvVars), `.templ`, `.ts`, `Dockerfile`, `go.mod`
# — and `Dockerfile` is extensionless, so no `*.ext` pattern could ever have
# reached it. A list of covered types is a list kept beside the truth: it goes
# stale on the next file type somebody adds, silently, and the gate written
# against it cannot see what it omits. Defaulting and carving out the exceptions
# inverts that — a new file type is covered on the commit that adds it.
#
# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles carry a harder consequence than a false alarm: a
# CRLF shebang makes the interpreter path end in \r, so the script fails to
# execute naming a binary that does not exist. And clients/claude-code/extensions
# /agentsmemory.ts is a shipped go:embed asset, so CRLF there travels to an
# operator rather than only failing a gate.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched, and `-text` is what actually stops it —
# `text=auto` GUESSES, and a wrong guess corrupts the file silently rather than
# failing. Listed explicitly so the guess is never consulted for these.
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.ico   -text
*.pdf   -text
*.gz    -text
*.zip   -text
*.wasm  -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text
